<article class="env-lemma" id="2878">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2878">Lemma <span data-tag="2878">5.5.6.11</span>.</a> Let $p: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a right fibration of $\infty $-categories, and let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ be a morphism in $\calC $. Then $f$ is $n$-truncated if and only if $p(f): p(X) \rightarrow p(Y)$ is $n$-truncated. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The map $\calC _{/Y} \rightarrow \calD _{/p(Y)}$ is a trivial fibration, and therefore an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>